//? Title: SJT permutations: actual largest-mobile adjacent swaps
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Generate all permutations while exchanging adjacent values once per transition.
Directions belong to values, and the largest mobile value determines the next
swap. The native producer records value positions while swapping.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Start1..n with every direction left. A value is mobile when its neighbor in its
direction exists and is smaller. Swap the largest mobile value, then reverse
directions of every larger value. Each successive permutation differs in exactly
one adjacent transposition; the complete stream has n! rows. This implementation
scans n positions per search, including the final failed search, so materialized
time and storage grow factorially. The empty permutation is one row.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/steinhaus_johnson_trotter_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/steinhaus_johnson_trotter.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::sjt_trace(3);
    std::print("| actual permutation | mobile | from | to | directions by value |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | " "---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.history)
        std::print("| `{}` | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n",
                   r.permutations[s.permutation_index], s.mobile, s.from, s.to,
                   s.directions);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Values1..3 initially point left");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual adjacent swaps",
                                     r.adjacent_swaps));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} emitted permutations",
                                     r.permutations.size()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/steinhaus_johnson_trotter_tiny.svg");
}
```
