> API and interpretation

Complete factorial output and copied histories are checked before generation.
Values must fit the int index representation. This is a materializing API, not a
constant-memory iterator. Actual position trajectories are producer output, not
report-side inverse-permutation reconstruction.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Johnson, Generation of Permutations by Adjacent Transposition, Mathematics of
  Computation17 (1963),282-285
- Trotter, Algorithm115: Perm, Communications of the ACM5 (1962),434-435

